│ Background (brief): Heart failure (HF) is a chronic disease that impacts quality of life and requires a complex      │
│ self-care regimen. Education is vital to support adherence. Traditional education is face-to-face using paper/video  │
│ materials. mHealth (mobile and wireless technologies) can deliver education via smartphones, tablets, SMS, apps,     │
│ web-based programs for mobile devices, and social media, potentially reaching people unable or unwilling to attend   │
│ traditional programs.                                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Objective: To systematically review and quantify benefits and harms of mHealth-delivered education for people with   │
│ HF.                                                                                                                  │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Selection criteria:                                                                                                  │
│ Include: Randomised controlled trials (RCTs) in adults (>=18) with diagnosed HF, comparing mHealth-delivered         │
│ education (e.g., smartphone/tablet apps, web-based education usable on mobile devices, SMS, social media, other      │
│ mobile device-delivered education) versus usual HF care.                                                             │
│ Exclude: Non-RCTs; non-HF populations; non-education or telemonitoring-only interventions without educational        │
│ content; purely face-to-face or paper/DVD-only programs; desktop-only web interventions not intended for mobile use. │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Instructions:                                                                                                        │
│ - Conduct ONLY title/abstract screening for EXACTLY the studies in this bounded chunk.                               │
│ - Make one screening decision per study in the chunk.                                                                │
