│ Review title: mHealth education interventions in heart failure                                                       │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Background (summary): Heart failure (HF) requires complex self-care. Education is vital. mHealth (mobile and         │
│ wireless technologies) can deliver HF education via smartphones, tablets, SMS, apps, and social media.               │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Objective: Systematically review benefits/harms of mHealth-delivered education for people with HF.                   │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Inclusion criteria (Title/Abstract stage):                                                                           │
│ - Study design: Randomised controlled trials (RCTs).                                                                 │
│ - Population: Adults (≥18 years) with a diagnosis of heart failure.                                                  │
│ - Intervention: mHealth-delivered education, e.g., internet/web-based programs for use on smartphones/tablets        │
│ (including apps), SMS text messaging, and social media–delivered education, or other mobile/wireless devices used to │
│ deliver educational content.                                                                                         │
│ - Comparator: Usual HF care (or equivalent standard care).                                                           │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Exclusion criteria (Title/Abstract stage):                                                                           │
│ - Non-RCTs (observational, quasi-experimental without randomization, qualitative, protocols without results).        │
│ - Population not primarily adults with HF, or mixed populations without clear HF subgroup at abstract level.         │
│ - Interventions that are not educational or not mHealth-based (e.g., telemonitoring-only without educational         │
│ component; telephone-only counseling without mobile/wireless tech; face-to-face only; paper/DVD-only without mobile  │
│ delivery; clinic- or desktop-only eHealth without mobile/wireless use).                                              │
│ - Interventions focused solely on medication/device therapy without an educational component delivered via mHealth.  │
│ - Pediatric populations.                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Ambiguity handling: If key RCT and HF and mHealth-education elements are plausibly present but unclear at abstract   │
│ level, lean toward inclusion.                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                      │
